{
  "info": {
    "name": "Bifrost V1 - Rate Limit / Budget",
    "description": "Rate limit and budget enforcement tests at the wire level. Request limit: VK with request_max_limit 2 allows exactly 2 usage-bearing requests and blocks the 3rd with 429 request_limited (enforcement compares with >=), then recovers after the 1m window. Token limit: token_max_limit 1 blocks the 2nd request with 429 token_limited. Budget: a tiny max_limit blocks with 402 budget_exceeded once cost accrues. Counters are read via GET /api/governance/virtual-keys/{id}?from_memory=true (immediate) - never via /api/governance/budgets, /rate-limits, or /quota, which lag behind the 10s DB dump ticker. Counter-dependent assertions are skip-guarded on priming success so the suite stays green when no provider key is configured. Deeper budget-cycle semantics (calendar alignment, overrides, multi-window) are covered by the Go suite in tests/governance (make test-governance).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
